ar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:58:37-07:00","id":734605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=734448#post734448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine. Lilith. Charon. Lucifer. Grandmother. Gaia. God.<br /> <br /> Done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Immensely helpful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T09:06:20-07:00","id":734924,"title":"","content":"A demon who belongs to the house of Devils, who is also an evangelistic preacher. traveling from town to town with his circus esque temple","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T09:10:03-07:00","id":734929,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused by what you're going for here. World of Darkness games really don't tend to be as focused on who can kill who, except in a dramatic story sense.<br /> <br /> But, I suppose you could use any Vampire who was Embraced as a child? That'd be generally unexpected, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:53:14-07:00","id":735919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=734929#post734929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused by what you're going for here. World of Darkness games really don't tend to be as focused on who can kill who, except in a dramatic story sense.<br /> <br /> But, I suppose you could use any Vampire who was Embraced as a child? That'd be generally unexpected, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit more of a trop\u00e9 if you ask me. Also, I'd argue most World of Darkness games focus pretty heavily on killing. It's almost kind of the point of Werewolf. Wraiths have endured a brutal killing just by being, and are constantly battling the forces of Oblivion and their shadow. Vampire very often becomes a political backstab off. And y'know... Hunter...<br /> <br /> But to clarify. Unexpectedly deadly or powerful character concepts or use of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T17:27:34-07:00","id":736352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=735919#post735919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bit more of a trop\u00e9 if you ask me. Also, I'd argue most World of Darkness games focus pretty heavily on killing. It's almost kind of the point of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off by a mile. Violence is a thing that Garou are very good at, making it an easy option for addressing problems. It just doesn't always really solve them in desirable ways. Additionally, violence can be considered a constant occupational hazard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wraiths have endured a brutal killing just by being, and are constantly battling the forces of Oblivion and their shadow </div> </div> </div>Only members of a specific cohort. Everyone else has disease, happenstance, accidents, etc.,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire very often becomes a political backstab off. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's more that another name for it could be &quot;Sexmurder&quot;, much as with Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And y'know... Hunter... </div> </div> </div>Also y'know, everyone who isn't an Avenger or Wayward. Hell, even they don't really have any guarantee of success when it comes to killing, and don't stop being squishy like any other human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:07:58-07:00","id":736633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=734605#post734605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Immensely helpful...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm joining the others in not really being sure what you're expecting us to say.<br /> <br /> You could min-max to produce a killing machine with a variety of concepts. Most of them will be pretty shallow, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:20:42-07:00","id":736655,"title":"","content":"I initially had this idea regarding Tzimisce Revenant families that lives in rural areas, like The Bratovitch, but I think that it can be applied to any character with Animalism. I wondered about the threat of werewolf attacks against the isolated castles or mansions of the Tzimisce or Revenants, depending on how much of an issue the ST wants to make that sort of thing. I thought that a good counter to that would be to keep a large number of dog ghouls around. These would be trained from birth and even bred over the generations to be particularly powerful and ferocious and the blood bond combined with Animalism would make them loyal and obedient beyond compare. There would be one additional plus for werewolf protection. They could have silver capped teeth. This might be made even more effective if this was done with the help of Vicissitude. You could also throw in silver spiked collars or dog barding. Dogs can be grown pretty quickly in large numbers, so this Tzimisce could have dozens of dogs like this in and around his compound. Not only would they make vicious combatants, but their heightened senses, especially scent, would help them to detect invaders as no human servants could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:30:11-07:00","id":736666,"title":"","content":"Ok, running through things:<br /> <br /> VtM - It's hard to be surprising here. Vampires are dangerous, and the Disciplines aren't hard to be creative with to make even the non-combat oriented ones things that can be very dangerous.<br /> <br /> WtA - Like vampires, werewolves are all pretty dangerous as a baseline. However, I think it's easier to be surprising her as Tribe and Auspice creates expectations on who's going to be the deadliest. If you want to really catch someone off guard? Child of Gaia Ragabash are exceedingly deadly; esp. once they hit Adren. They're not at their best in a stand up fight (they are Ragabash after all) but they're no chumps there, and you can build one that can easily deal 12-15 levels of Agg damage with a successful attack (and Ragabash sneak is very helpful).<br /> <br /> Totem selection can also really change how characters perform. The right Totem can easily take a splat combo that doesn't seem that strong and make them devastating by WtA standards (if you have a group willing to deal with the Ban, Hummingbird turns non-combat PCs into monsters with ease, for example).<br /> <br /> WtO - Like VtM, it's hard to be surprisingly deadly. The &quot;good at being deadly&quot; options are pretty straighforward.<br /> <br /> CtD - CtD is sort of the opposite of VtM/WtO. While it has some obvious combat Kiths, Arts and Realms are flexible and widely available enough that any changeling can whip out some of the deadly options. Since there's little expectations, there's little surprise to achieve. I've found the most success I've had in that regard was a Childling Satyr (think a character that basically sees Jack Sparrow as an idol), simply because &quot;so crazy and naive about how fighting works,&quot; isn't something people expect from that splat combo.<br /> <br /> MtR - Again, the &quot;deadly&quot; options are pretty straightforward. You're not going to get surprised by any of the deadlier combinations of traits.<br /> <br /> HtR - Generally, Mercy and non-Wayward Vision Creeds surprise people. Though really I don't know why, there's plenty of obviously deadly stuff in their arsenals; for Hunters anyway. And you can pick up Edges from other Creeds as it is.<br /> <br /> Orpheus - Again, it's not really that surprising where you're going to find the most deadly stuff, but Orpheus has some surprising things with how Nature, Shade, and Lament interact. I don't remember some of the combos, but you can easily boost Spite or Vitality pretty high with them, letting you use some of powers with much more strength than people might imagine at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T09:37:49-07:00","id":738638,"title":"","content":"I think I figured out where I'm confused. When you're talking about characters that are surprisingly deadly, do you mean surprising for the players, as in a character combination that shouldn't have worked very well but did? Or surprising for other characters, such as someone who consistently gets underestimated within the game?<br /> <br /> I've seen some players do surprising things with characters like very high generation caitiff or thin blood. Not even in the obvious &quot;new discipline&quot; power game sense. But a vampire able to wake up during the day or operate in even dim/overcast sunlight has a considerable advantage when it comes to setting up an assassination or ambush.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T16:39:34-07:00","id":740001,"title":"","content":"any demon that knows the ritual to spit out burning spectres?<br /> <br /> a geneticist devourer demon that has collected a multitude of different animal forms and has mastered beast lore<br /> <br /> it really depends on what form of deadly you are going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T19:47:18-08:00","id":748242,"title":"","content":"a gangrel with a ghouled mountain gorilla. had a bunch of machetes tied to him, like those roosters they use in cock fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T12:16:33-08:00","id":749688,"title":"","content":"I've often thought to myself that for someone with Animalism ghouling an elephant or rhino would have many of the tactical benefits of creating a vohzd without the concerns about breaking the Masquerade or being overpowered and eaten by one's own ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T13:39:01-08:00","id":749979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=749688#post749688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've often thought to myself that for someone with Animalism ghouling an elephant or rhino would have many of the tactical benefits of creating a vohzd without the concerns about breaking the Masquerade or being overpowered and eaten by one's own ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Want to hear my version of what a rhinopeed is? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T01:02:17-08:00","id":750920,"title":"","content":"Ha, ghouling and animalism seems to create some pretty weird stuff, Tzimisce Anti-Werewolf hounds, Gangrel Mountain Gorilla friends and Elephant and Rhino pals are pretty all pretty amusing.<br /> <br /> Nagah gifts seem to stack in some silly ways. It's like nobody ever really thought about how some of the math pools would interact. I managed to make one churn out 50+ levels of Agg damage per action (action, not round), from 30 feet away, for a thought exercise the other day. I expect Were-creatures to be fighty, but being more lethal than an actual Nuclear Weapon in the setting was a little, &quot;Well then.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:43:32-08:00","id":753072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=750920#post750920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha, ghouling and animalism seems to create some pretty weird stuff, Tzimisce Anti-Werewolf hounds, Gangrel Mountain Gorilla friends and Elephant and Rhino pals are pretty all pretty amusing.<br /> <br /> Nagah gifts seem to stack in some silly ways. It's like nobody ever really thought about how some of the math pools would interact. I managed to make one churn out 50+ levels of Agg damage per action (action, not round), from 30 feet away, for a thought exercise the other day. I expect Were-creatures to be fighty, but being more lethal than an actual Nuclear Weapon in the setting was a little, &quot;Well then.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuclear weapons would be plot devices, not necessarily quantifiable levels of damage for the purposes of the game. Also, if you want to max out Nagah deadliness, the go-to Traits are actually Dexterity and Performance, with a specialty in dancing for the Rank 6 Gift Dance of Shiva. At 21 successes, the theoretical maximum you'll typically see, you can cover most of the world (a radius of roughly <i>5,958 miles</i>, which is about half again the radius of the Earth) in flames dealing 25 dice of fire damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-04-2015, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T00:59:38-08:00","id":753355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=753072#post753072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nuclear weapons would be plot devices, not necessarily quantifiable levels of damage for the purposes of the game. Also, if you want to max out Nagah deadliness, the go-to Traits are actually Dexterity and Performance, with a specialty in dancing for the Rank 6 Gift Dance of Shiva. At 21 successes, the theoretical maximum you'll typically see, you can cover most of the world (a radius of roughly <i>5,958 miles</i>, which is about half again the radius of the Earth) in flames dealing 25 dice of fire damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I distinctly remember reading somewhere that Nuclear Devices at their centre do 30 levels of Unsoakable Aggravated damage. But I can't remember exactly where I read this. Hmm... I'll take a look later. I know Mummy the Resurrection describes being at their centre as being one of the few things that'll permanently destroy a Mummy.<br /> <br /> ...Dance of Shiva though, wow. Now that's rules silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T02:48:31-08:00","id":753489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=753072#post753072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nuclear weapons would be plot devices, not necessarily quantifiable levels of damage for the purposes of the game. Also, if you want to max out Nagah deadliness, the go-to Traits are actually Dexterity and Performance, with a specialty in dancing for the Rank 6 Gift Dance of Shiva. At 21 successes, the theoretical maximum you'll typically see, you can cover most of the world (a radius of roughly <i>5,958 miles</i>, which is about half again the radius of the Earth) in flames dealing 25 dice of fire damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly surprisingly deadly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=753355#post753355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly remember reading somewhere that Nuclear Devices at their centre do 30 levels of Unsoakable Aggravated damage. But I can't remember exactly where I read this. Hmm... I'll take a look later. I know Mummy the Resurrection describes being at their centre as being one of the few things that'll permanently destroy a Mummy.<br /> <br /> ...Dance of Shiva though, wow. Now that's rules silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember reading it anywhere, but I haven't read all the books. Clearly, the Ravnos antediluvian was able to soak nuclear damage during the Week of Nightmares, though. That could be due to a high-level custom Fortitude level or some other power, so who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-04-2015, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T05:01:25-08:00","id":753714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=753355#post753355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I distinctly remember reading somewhere that Nuclear Devices at their centre do 30 levels of Unsoakable Aggravated damage. But I can't remember exactly where I read this. Hmm... I'll take a look later. I know Mummy the Resurrection describes being at their centre as being one of the few things that'll permanently destroy a Mummy.<br /> <br /> ...Dance of Shiva though, wow. Now that's rules silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, It's just rank 6 for the incarnations of Death. Feels just fine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:17:06-08:00","id":753830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts#post733132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys,<br /> <br /> For a challenge, I'm looking for inspiration on how to create a character that is extraordinarily lethal, in the most unorthodox or innocent manner possible. The race can be anything except Kuei-Jin or Mage. I'm looking for unorthodox and out of the box ideas. Maybe share some of your previous character concepts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Werewolf with rabies who's regenerative powers stops the disease from killing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:49:50-08:00","id":754287,"title":"","content":"Addendum for Dance of Shiva: that's the radius of effect and damage you reach after 21 turns of dancing. It starts off slow and short, at 4 dice and 10 yards. Every successive turn, it adds a die and doubles the distance. <b>Also, there is no cost to use it</b>. It arguably comes out ahead of the Yin Prana 8 alternative power of the same name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/733132-surprisingly-deadly-character-concepts?p=753714#post753714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, It's just rank 6 for the incarnations of Death. Feels just fine.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the few Rank 6 Gifts that is actually an overtly powerful effect. Others tend to be rather subtle and only kind of potent in comparison, like being able to break out of any bindings or heal non-silver aggravated damage as if it were lethal, both as permanent enhancements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-04-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T22:50:08-08:00","id":758061,"title":"","content":"A vampire (or better yet, a zombie) stuffed full of plastic explosives. Maybe with vials of some deadly bioweapon mixed in as shrapnel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:34:45-08:00","id":759182,"title":"","content":"For out right lethality from character generation, I would say the most dangerous build I have seen was an Assamite Sniper build who also was trained in demolitions.<br /> <br /> Quietus level 1 means you are a walking sound suppressor that can completely negate the sound of any gun or if you are close enough any explosion. So you can fire an M95 or similar 50 cal. rifle and not make a sound. It also means you can use directional claymore mines to protect your back in a sniper hide.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate ensures that your sniper hide is perfect against anything except Auspex, though since most decent sniper rifles can hit a target over a mile away, even if the target is some how aware that there is a sniper in the area and they have Auspex, chances are that they won't think to look that far away and by the time they do look that far you will have already taken the head shot.<br /> <br /> The 50 cal. rifle ammo also provides a few benefits you don't get with normal guns in cWoD games. They are big enough to use Assamite blood poisons on, especially if you do custom sealed hollow point rounds. Failing that there are many real world specialty ammunition types that can enhance the lethality of such a weapon. Everything from armor penetration that cuts through manhole covers or walls to phosphorus rounds (tracers) to burn undead targets.<br /> <br /> The catch about this build is that both the player and the ST need to have an above average understanding of guns, ammo and sniping techniques to bring out its potential. With such a setup a lone character generation Assamite can solo many enemies that would take team tactics to over come. If you build a coterie with complementary skills and tactics, then they can steam roller most opponents.<br /> <br /> It would be tempting to say that just the player needs to have this knowledge, but in truth the ST needs it as well because such a character forces the game to change tone and scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:10:26-08:00","id":759545,"title":"","content":"Fun with Create Element: get someone to plant a shitload of flour or sawdust around where you'll be fighting. Make sure it gets spread around, possibly with supplement use of certain Wendigo Gifts. Then light it up. Discount fuel-air explosion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T21:26:33-08:00","id":759703,"title":"","content":"The Assamite sniper concept (besides where we want to quibble about the surprising factor of a Clan known for being assassins) is better served with lower powered weapons.<br /> <br /> A supersonic round is going to make sound on its own once it exits Quietus' zone of silence. Sure, it will help you out, but a subsonic around will actually be completely silenced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T04:18:07-08:00","id":759889,"title":"","content":"Assamite sniper just also isn't particularly lethal compared to, say a starting Nagah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}